  "intent": "Write a ~350-word grounded explainer on why lithium-ion batteries lose capacity over time and what that means for the lifespan of wireless earbuds. Take the technical grounding from English Wikipedia (__WIKIPEDIA__), at least one real owner thread from Postmill (__REDDIT__) describing battery decline, and the listed battery/runtime spec from one earbud product page on the One Stop Market (__SHOPPING__). Cite every factual claim as a markdown [label](url) link to sandbox-local pages you actually opened. The report must cover (1) charge-cycle and thermal aging mechanisms (from Wikipedia), (2) the practical consequence for the small cell in a real earbud product (anchor this to the product page's stated battery/runtime spec), and (3) at least one forum owner's reported battery-life decline. Answer starts with the report in Markdown; no chain-of-thought.",
